{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue was in `median()` in `repo/stats.py`. Report column summaries go through `stats_summary()` in `repo/rows.py`, which calls that function.\n\nFor lists with an **even** length, the implementation used the lower of the two middle values instead of their average. Odd-length lists were already correct.\n\n**Before:** `return s[mid] if n % 2 else s[mid - 1]` — e.g. `[1, 2, 3, 4]` → `2`  \n**After:** average the two middle values — e.g. `[1, 2, 3, 4]` → `2.5`\n\nAll tests in `tests/visible/test_stats.py` pass. Columns with an even number of data points should now show the correct median."}]},"session_id":"e1af0775-5792-46ca-ab36-37cc08c28a19"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":34477,"duration_api_ms":34477,"is_error":false,"result":"Searching the codebase for how report medians are calculated.\n\n\nIdentifying the bug: for even-length lists the median returns the lower-middle element instead of averaging the two middle values.\n\n\nThe issue was in `median()` in `repo/stats.py`. Report column summaries go through `stats_summary()` in `repo/rows.py`, which calls that function.\n\nFor lists with an **even** length, the implementation used the lower of the two middle values instead of their average. Odd-length lists were already correct.\n\n**Before:** `return s[mid] if n % 2 else s[mid - 1]` — e.g. `[1, 2, 3, 4]` → `2`  \n**After:** average the two middle values — e.g. `[1, 2, 3, 4]` → `2.5`\n\nAll tests in `tests/visible/test_stats.py` pass. Columns with an even number of data points should now show the correct median.","session_id":"e1af0775-5792-46ca-ab36-37cc08c28a19","request_id":"ac5f3ee1-3307-4342-a9b2-542ad75a5991","usage":{"inputTokens":11818,"outputTokens":1030,"cacheReadTokens":47001,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
